00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.640
The core satellite ETF approach builds a low-cost, broad market core with tactical satellite

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.300
positions that target specific themes or sectors.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:27.040
Today's market conditions with mixed-rate signals and sector rotation make this structure

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.040
relevant because the core provides stability while satellites capture opportunities like

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.560
the TSX miners that lifted the index.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:41.980
A Canadian investor can implement it in a TFSA by allocating 70% to XIC as the core

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:49.020
for broad Canadian exposure, and 30% to sector ETFs such as those tracking utilities or technology.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:54.840
Historical data shows this method performed best during periods of sector leadership shifts

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.800
when rebalancing occurred quarterly rather than monthly to control transaction costs.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:05.900
Risks include over-concentration in satellites if the core allocation drifts below 60%.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.320
Use a platform like WealthSimple or Questrade to set automatic rebalancing alerts

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:15.240
reports, when any satellite exceeds its target weight by 5%.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:20.520
Track performance against the TSX composite to confirm the satellites are adding alpha,

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:24.280
without increasing overall volatility beyond the core alone.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:31.160
The XIC ETF itself trades with tight spreads that support frequent small adjustments inside

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:35.220
registered accounts without eroding returns through wide bid-ask gaps.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:40.900
Sector satellites can be sized in fixed dollar amounts rather than percentages so that

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:45.840
rebalancing triggers only when the core weight moves beyond the 5% drift threshold.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:51.380
Quarterly rebalancing has historically kept transaction costs below the alpha generated

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.240
by timely sector exposure during rotation periods.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:04:00.200
The approach separates the stable Canadian market beta from opportunistic bets on themes such

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.060
such as utilities or technology that may outperform during specific policy cycles.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:11.420
Imagine you bought XIC last week when the TSX rallied on mining gains and your order

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:12.680
filled at the market price.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:18.380
The mechanism that actually determines your cost is the ETF's creation redemption process,

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:23.960
which keeps the price within one or two basis points of net asset value even during volatile

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:24.480
sessions.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:29.940
Most retail investors do not realize that holding the core in a registered account like

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:36.480
a TFSA avoids annual capital gains distributions that can erode returns in non-registered accounts.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.020
The pro tip is to set satellite positions at fixed dollar amounts rather than percentages,

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:47.120
so rebalancing happens only when the core drifts more than 5% from target.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:53.000
The common misconception is that frequent satellite trading improves returns when the real

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.880
edge comes from keeping the core allocation stable and letting the satellites run until

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:03.380
they hit a predefined exit rule, such as a 20% gain or a sector rotation signal.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.760
The creation redemption arbitrage keeps tracking error low enough that even a 5% satellite

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:15.400
allocation can be added or removed without moving the overall portfolio beta outside its

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.220
intended range.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:21.540
Registered account placement of the core also shields the investor from the annual tax

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:26.820
drag that appears when the same ETF sits in a taxable brokerage account during high distribution

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:32.480
years. Fixed dollar satellite sizing removes the need for constant percentage calculations,

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:38.120
and instead triggers a review only when the core weight moves beyond the 5% drift threshold.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:44.020
Exit rules tied to absolute gains or sector signals prevent the common error of holding a

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:49.960
satellite too long after its original catalyst has faded. This is a simulated trade for educational

